\"font-size:.95em; margin-top:1em\"><br><div style=\"color:#6b095d; border-left:1px solid #d0d0d0; margin:0 .5em; padding:0 .6em\"><div>On Fri, 18 Sep 2026 11:55:20 GMT Purchasing wrote:</div><br><blockquote dir=\"auto\" style=\"font-style:normal; margin:0; padding:0\">Hi,<span><br></span>I received an email about your application security audits and wanted to understand a bit more about what the service offers.<span><br></span>When I looked into it, it appeared to be focused primarily on monitoring and testing website applications, and I wasn't sure how this would apply to our setup.<span><br></span>Our main systems are Microsoft 365, Dropbox, and Asana, along with a single DNS entry that points to an AI application hosted on a VPS. Other than that, I'm not aware of any additional applications that would fall into the category of web applications.<span><br></span>We are interested in improving our security posture and would likely benefit from a penetration test, but when I previously reviewed the audit process, I remember being asked a number of highly technical questions that I wasn't able to answer. I also got the impression that the service was limited to website or web application security and didn't extend to the wider systems we use.<span><br></span>Could you help me understand what value we could gain from the platform given our environment, and whether it can assess or provide recommendations beyond public-facing websites and web applications? If so, I'd be happy to revisit it.<span><br></span>Many Thanks,<span><br></span><span><br></span>Giles<span><br></span><span><br></span>Purchasing Manager<span><br></span><span><br></span>Sesame Access Systems Ltd<span><br></span><span><br></span>Unit 1, Cumberland Works<span><br></span><span><br></span>Wintersells Business Park<span><br></span><span><br></span>West Byfleet<span><br></span><span><br></span>Surrey<span><br></span><span><br></span>United Kingdom<span><br></span><span><br></span>KT14 7LF<span><br></span